      "content": "Focusing on appearance and demeanor is crucial for early identification. Officers should be alert to individuals wearing clothing that is overly tactical or that conceals body shape, as this can suggest intent to carry weapons. Certain groups congregating in areas where they don't typically belong, especially if they are exhibiting a unified, watchful behavior, warrants closer observation. Finally, a stiff, overly deliberate gait or a constant scanning of the environment can signal a heightened state of readiness or paranoia.",
